Compare national occupations that overlap with commercial analytics work. These benchmarks include all industries and experience levels; they are not expected certificate starting salaries.

BLS · 2025–2035 projections · May 2025 wages

benchmarks = FileAttachment("outputs/us-employer-inventory/web/outlook-data.json").json()
occupations = benchmarks.occupations
metricLabels = new Map([["Projected growth (%)", "growth"], ["Median annual wage ($)", "median"], ["Annual projected openings", "openings"]])
formatMetric = (value, key) =&gt; key === "median" ? "$" + value.toLocaleString("en-US") : key === "growth" ? value + "%" : value.toLocaleString("en-US")
comparison = occupations.filter(d =&gt; selectedOccupations.includes(d.name)).sort((a, b) =&gt; b[metric] - a[metric])





































Choose your comparison

viewof selectedOccupations = Inputs.checkbox(occupations.map(d =&gt; d.name), {label: "Occupations", value: occupations.map(d =&gt; d.name)})
viewof metric = Inputs.select(metricLabels, {label: "Compare", value: "growth"})


















Occupation comparison

comparison.length ? html`&lt;div class="outlook-grid"&gt;${comparison.map(d =&gt; html`&lt;article class="benchmark-card"&gt;
  &lt;span class="tiny"&gt;SOC ${d.soc} · NATIONAL PROXY&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;h3&gt;${d.name}&lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;strong class="benchmark-growth"&gt;${metric === "growth" && d.growth &gt; 0 ? "+" : ""}${formatMetric(d[metric], metric)}&lt;/strong&gt;
  &lt;p class="tiny"&gt;${metric === "growth" ? `projected growth, ${benchmarks.projection_period}` : metric === "median" ? `May ${benchmarks.wage_year} median annual wage` : `average annual projected openings, ${benchmarks.projection_period}`}&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;div class="growth-track" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;span style=${`width:${100 * d[metric] / Math.max(1, ...occupations.map(o =&gt; o[metric]))}%`}&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="benchmark-facts"&gt;
    &lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;${formatMetric(d.median, "median")}&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;small&gt;Median annual wage&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;${formatMetric(d.openings, "openings")}&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;small&gt;Annual projected openings&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;p class="tiny"&gt;${d.growth}% projected growth · ${benchmarks.projection_period}. Openings include replacement needs, not currently advertised jobs.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;a href=${d.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;BLS source ↗&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=${d.onet} target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;O*NET occupation ↗&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;`)}&lt;/div&gt;` : html`&lt;p role="status"&gt;Select at least one occupation to compare.&lt;/p&gt;`







Change the measure to update the highlighted figures and comparison tracks. Cards and the table follow your occupation selection. Tracks use the highest value across all benchmark occupations, so filtering does not change their scale.




